  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) is inscribed in circle \\(\\odot O\\). Point \\(A\\) lies on the major arc \\(BD\\), and \\(\\angle BOD=140^\\circ\\). Find \\(\\angle C\\) (in degrees).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "110",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\angle A=\\angle BOD\\div 2=70^\\circ\\). Opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral are supplementary, so \\(\\angle C=180^\\circ-70^\\circ=110^\\circ\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the major arc directly\n\nThe opposite vertices \\(A\\) and \\(C\\) lie on opposite arcs with endpoints \\(B,D\\). Since \\(A\\) lies on the major arc \\(BD\\), \\(C\\) lies on the minor arc, so \\(\\angle C\\) intercepts the major arc. This arc measures \\(360^\\circ-140^\\circ=220^\\circ\\). By the inscribed angle theorem,\n\\[\n\\angle C=\\frac{220^\\circ}{2}=110^\\circ.\n\\]",
